# Reusable components

In this repository, UI reuse is implemented mainly through tag files in
`WEB-INF/tags`, not through `jsp:include` files inside a `components/` folder.

The default rule is to abstract duplicated frontend code whenever it is reasonable.
Repeated markup, repeated class combinations, and repeated interaction patterns
should be extracted into reusable components so the codebase keeps as little
duplication as practical.

## Real structure

```
webapp/src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/
|- views/
|  |- index.jsp
|  |- marketplace.jsp
|  |- nuevo/item-detail.jsp
|  `- helloworld/index.jsp
`- tags/
   |- button.tag
   |- card.tag
   `- heading.tag
```

## Correct taglibs

In views:

```jsp
<%@ taglib prefix="c" uri="http://java.sun.com/jsp/jstl/core" %>
<%@ taglib prefix="paw" tagdir="/WEB-INF/tags" %>
```

In tag files:

```jsp
<%@ tag language="java" pageEncoding="UTF-8" %>
<%@ attribute name="text" required="true" %>
<%@ taglib prefix="c" uri="http://java.sun.com/jsp/jstl/core" %>
```

Do not document `core_rt` or a `WEB-INF/jsp/components` folder, because they do
not match the real repository.

## How they are used

```jsp
<paw:heading level="1" text="Botecito" />
<paw:button text="Principal" color="primary" />
<paw:card name="Producto A" price="1500" date="17/03/2026" />
```

## How they are implemented

Tag files define attributes and encapsulate reusable markup. Real examples:

- `heading.tag` receives `level`, `text`, and `cssClass`.
- `button.tag` receives `text`, `color`, `size`, `cssClass`, and `disabled`.
- `card.tag` receives `name`, `price`, `date`, `imgSrc`, and `cssClass`.

Use more reusable primitives such as:

- form field wrappers;
- input, textarea, select, and checkbox components;
- modal, drawer, dropdown, badge, alert, and empty-state components;
- layout primitives such as page headers, sections, stacks, and grids.

If a repeated interaction also needs JavaScript, keep the markup reusable and move
the interaction logic to a minimal shared script instead of duplicating inline code.

## Rules

- Reuse `WEB-INF/tags` before duplicating large blocks across multiple JSPs.
- If a piece of UI appears more than once, strongly consider extracting it.
- Use JSTL and EL expressions; do not use scriptlets.
- Keep UI logic inside the tag file and business logic out of the view layer.
- Use `<c:url>` for links and resources.
- Keep repeated styling in shared CSS classes instead of repeating long utility sets
  across many views when a reusable abstraction is clearer.
